{"title":"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2(Probably_the_easiest)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2(Probably the easiest)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(bash_for_life)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (bash for life)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/b/7db4abece4325c0937ce81e30e3f6906f04be95e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)=1-\\dfrac{1}{3}x+\\dfrac{1}{6}x^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"169\" height=\"37\" />, define\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/6/fa6f39b1ace558af03317c51070236a86d7110ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)=P(x)P(x^{3})P(x^{5})P(x^{7})P(x^{9})=\\sum_{i=0}^{50} a_ix^{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"369\" height=\"50\" />.\nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/f/35f9d890b18eb5fea33546dde0f5317355e835ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=0}^{50} |a_i|=\\dfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"96\" height=\"50\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7dfd17dc4d3100462df726e8eb7f9262783429eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> substitutes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/9/e1925ebd000383fb695b421ebd5ef3769f1e79ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x^3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"21\" /> substitutes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48524d3889ec8433cb03669176e738011df245b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84fc073a22692e60ed61118e1c39da81dff6cd00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x^5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"21\" /> substitutes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/7/077791531216b77f911a9821f320c1924efafb7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^5$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, etc. Notice how this doesn't change the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />. So, the sum of the absolute values of the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/9/e1925ebd000383fb695b421ebd5ef3769f1e79ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x^3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84fc073a22692e60ed61118e1c39da81dff6cd00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x^5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8f85e583ad5680e21f5eb8e190e21e059e9f88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x^7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/7/53767d1d13d9f3e53bea2e633d1e6d6b23ad2edd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x^9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"21\" /> are all the same. The sum of the absolute values of the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e5979a3d2ddfb438d6923ee289ee6d2c55f127d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{3} + 1 = \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, the sum of the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/0/180c4dfc2a9778b3322128d58225b1cc31a490a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^5 = \\frac{243}{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"337\" height=\"48\" />, in which we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/0/d109b1ec2ec36bb0e3e71f552fcf5afed064f7d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$243+32 = \\boxed{275}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2.28Probably_the_easiest.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2(Probably_the_easiest)\">Solution 2(Probably the easiest)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2(Probably the easiest)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that all the coefficients of odd-powered terms is an odd number of odd degree terms multiplied together, and all coefficients of even-powered terms have an even number of odd degree terms multiplied together. Since every odd degree term is negative, and every even degree term is positive, the sum is just equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/d/6fddc6cfb6449dfa85f3aec556cc85a7771fb4ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(-1)=P(-1)^{5}=\\left( \\dfrac{3}{2}\\right)^{5}=\\dfrac{243}{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"259\" height=\"46\" />, so the desired answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f2958311bb0a577984a7ceb6da129597028840cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$243+32=\\boxed{275}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>[YINGLINWU] Just a quick comment: After multiplying out the product for Q(x) into the sum of monomials, the coefficient of a monomial of even degree is always positive while the coefficient of a monomial of odd degree is always negative. Therefore, as we are collecting similar terms, no coefficients of monomials cancel out. It follows that the sum of absolute values of coefficients of Q(x) is the same as that of Q(-x), which is given by Q(-1).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are looking for the sum of the absolute values of the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />. By defining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/2/3b24c66a665f19ad635713d86c08a9add00e6a12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;(x) = 1 + \\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{1}{6}x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"174\" height=\"37\" />, and defining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed2194244fb98ed143dd070cf2c2072ac557fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q&#39;(x) = P&#39;(x)P&#39;(x^3)P&#39;(x^5)P&#39;(x^7)P&#39;(x^9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"313\" height=\"19\" />, we have made it so that all coefficients in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/827261955d01e0b91631bb4756c806bfb75a2673.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q&#39;(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> are just the positive/absolute values of the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />. . \n</p><p><br />\nTo find the sum of the absolute values of the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, we can just take the sum of the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/827261955d01e0b91631bb4756c806bfb75a2673.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q&#39;(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" />. This sum is equal to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/7/507271d1f2043b3d858e5bd017b7e309a552eb79.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q&#39;(1) = P&#39;(1)P&#39;(1)P&#39;(1)P&#39;(1)P&#39;(1) = \\left(1+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{6}\\right)^5 = \\frac{243}{32},\\]\" width=\"473\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/0/d109b1ec2ec36bb0e3e71f552fcf5afed064f7d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$243+32 = \\boxed{275}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Note: this method doesn't work for every product of polynomials. Example: The sum of the absolute values of the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793b6ec68906828fcb6d26a5455b1d677b30a14c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K(x) = (2x^2 - 6x - 5)(10x - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"252\" height=\"19\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/2/f52872b2faf29d4c2ac1245bffb6109fb0b8f83b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$131$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> but when you find the sum of the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/8/cc8179f3b39fe02df7113f75c6054b5901089e56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K&#39;(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/d/ddd99be55541d127073003e3bf3860a1f37a8073.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K&#39;(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, then you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f61021f12ab09c5b9c3cfbcd7f6207920ff765b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$143$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. - whatRthose\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28bash_for_life.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(bash_for_life)\">Solution 4 (bash for life)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (bash for life)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We expand and add the numbers (I made two very easy mistakes and fixed them).\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://cdn.artofproblemsolving.com/attachments/1/6/c4e3bea5cf2d5bb7d7796049b5dc17fcd8a2ba.jpg\">https://cdn.artofproblemsolving.com/attachments/1/6/c4e3bea5cf2d5bb7d7796049b5dc17fcd8a2ba.jpg</a>\n</p><p>-maxamc\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II\" title=\"2016 AIME II\">2016 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2016\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017025255\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.044 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 289/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7779/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.203      1 -total\n 58.96%    7.785      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.44%    5.207      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14881:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017025255 and revision id 292791. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}